#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:1
msgid "Release 2.13 (2023-01-17)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:3
msgid ""
"The `repeat` and `enforce-determinism` options have been removed since they "
"had been broken under many circumstances for a long time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:6
msgid ""
"You can now use [flake references](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake."
"md#flake-references) in the [old command line interface](../command-ref/main-"
"commands.md), e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:18
msgid ""
"Instead of \"antiquotation\", the more common term [string interpolation](../"
"language/string-interpolation.md) is now used consistently. Historical "
"release notes were not changed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:21
msgid ""
"Error traces have been reworked to provide detailed explanations and more "
"accurate error locations. A short excerpt of the trace is now shown by "
"default when an error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:25
msgid ""
"Allow explicitly selecting outputs in a store derivation installable, just "
"like we can do with other sorts of installables. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:30
msgid "now works just as"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:34
msgid "does already."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:36
msgid ""
"On Linux, `nix develop` now sets the [_personality_](https://man7.org/linux/"
"man-pages/man2/personality.2.html) for the development shell in the same way "
"as the actual build of the derivation. This makes shells for `i686-linux` "
"derivations work correctly on `x86_64-linux`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:42
msgid ""
"You can now disable the global flake registry by setting the `flake-"
"registry` configuration option to an empty string. The same can be achieved "
"at runtime with `--flake-registry \"\"`."
msgstr ""
